Zero OS0.10.0 final integrated image: PASS on all four boot paths.

ISO: build/zero.iso, 18890752 bytes
SHA256:8f31413952cbac47c16074ef6fb6534ada173246f822916e54d79b35d9ffb129
Modes: BIOS64, BIOS32 without LM/PAE, UEFI64, UEFI32 without LM.
All tests used actual emulated PS/2 keyboard input; no guest code injection.
All four VMs stopped. Canonical ISO/user images and all eight private storage
fixture copies retained their complete hashes. See results.json and each
mode's result.json, actions.jsonl, session.txt, argv.json and disk hash lists.

Baseline includes automatic DHCP before any input, actual PCnet packets,
one-based thread/pixel bounds, independent graphics pause/resume, cable-loss
address clearing and automatic recovery while computation is paused, local
HTTP, public DNS resolving the local HTTP fixture, independent IPv4/TCP
checksums, real no-adapter WiFi modal input/Escape, native Zero/Ezero bundled
compile-and-run, error recovery,4095-byte output cap,64-bit integer semantics,
and read-only ZeroFS/ext4 volume access with one-based disk labels.

Sixteen additional checks per mode passed (0.10-extra.json): Ezero host()==0;
Zero guest argcount/argument primitives return0; Ezero arguments/read/write/
exists each report line1 and exit65 because host APIs are unavailable;
guarded portable branch and subsequent normal arithmetic work. Actual apps
menu, system monitor, volume selection and network applications work through
arrow/Enter/Backspace/Escape, including DHCP reconnection while computation
is paused, WiFi handoff, worker resume, direct commands, bad arguments and
preservation of terminal history/selected volume.

Nineteen actual1920x1080 PNG captures per mode are retained. Representative
UEFI64 images: applications-menu.png, system-computation-paused.png,
storage-selected-b.png, network-app-connected.png, wifi-real-status.png.
Menu and BIOS32 network images were also visually inspected: final KEYBOARD
APPS label, one-based entries, readable bounds, actual leased addresses.

Scope: QEMU/SeaBIOS/OVMF, not physical hardware or native VirtualBox. Wireless
tests cover honest no-radio handling, not association with real WiFi hardware.
HTTP peer is the local test server; public DNS itself is exercised. Guest
programs remain cooperative in the kernel address space; no isolation claim.

Two preliminary attempts are preserved separately. One corrected a missing
tilde mapping in the external PS/2 helper; the other replaced an invalid
unquoted phrase containing reserved builtin name host with valid arithmetic.
No product code or ISO changed during those fixture corrections. The final
complete rerun above passed on the exact same frozen ISO.
